<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>netstandard2.0</TargetFramework>
    <PackageType>MSBuildSdk</PackageType>
    <IncludeBuildOutput>false</IncludeBuildOutput>
    <IncludeSymbols>false</IncludeSymbols>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
    <PackageDescription>MSBuild SDK for Clavus — auto-selects packages and emits bootstrapping based on host SDK</PackageDescription>
    <PackageTags>$(PackageTags);sdk;msbuild</PackageTags>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Remove="Sdk/**" />
    <None Include="Sdk/**" Pack="true" PackagePath="Sdk/" />
    <Using Remove="**" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <!--
    Rocket.Surgery.ModularPipelines.Extensions' PackSolution module packs the whole solution with a
    single "dotnet pack, include symbols" invocation, which sets IncludeSymbols=true as an MSBuild
    global property. Global properties cannot be overridden by IncludeSymbols=false above, so a
    .snupkg is always attempted for this project. Because IncludeBuildOutput=false, the main
    package's lib/ output group is empty (by design — this is a content-only MSBuild SDK package,
    not a referenceable library), and NuGet's default debug-symbols output group is gated behind
    that same IncludeBuildOutput condition, so the .snupkg ends up with zero files and pack fails
    with NU5017 ("Cannot create a package that has no dependencies nor content").

    Fix: NuGet.Build.Tasks.Pack.targets' _GetDebugSymbolsWithTfm target adds an unconditional
    ItemGroup for TfmSpecificDebugSymbolsFile items, independent of IncludeBuildOutput, populated
    via the TargetsForTfmSpecificDebugSymbolsInPackage extension point. We use it to point the
    symbols package at the .pdb this project already produces during a normal build (it still
    compiles a trivial assembly even with no non-Sdk source files), giving the .snupkg legitimate
    content without adding a lib/ folder to the main package.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetsForTfmSpecificDebugSymbolsInPackage>$(TargetsForTfmSpecificDebugSymbolsInPackage);_ClavusSdkAddDebugSymbolsToPackage</TargetsForTfmSpecificDebugSymbolsInPackage>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <Target Name="_ClavusSdkAddDebugSymbolsToPackage" DependsOnTargets="Build">
    <ItemGroup>
      <TfmSpecificDebugSymbolsFile Include="$(TargetDir)$(TargetName).pdb" Condition="Exists('$(TargetDir)$(TargetName).pdb')">
        <TargetFramework>$(TargetFramework)</TargetFramework>
      </TfmSpecificDebugSymbolsFile>
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>
</Project>
